IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI
CASE NO: W.P. (Crl.) No. 310 of 2021
CITATION: 2021 SCC OnLine Del 3412
YEAR: 2021

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.N. Patel, Jasmeet Singh

PARTIES:
Foundation for Independent Journalism vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Information Technology Act, 2000

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 87 IT Act, IT Rules 2021

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
it rules 2021, digital media ethics, executive oversight, press freedom

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Examined the constitutional validity of Part III of the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021 regarding digital news publishers.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 87 IT Act, IT Rules 2021.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

